> Greg Lindahl wrote:
> > > void f(int x) {
> > >       (x ? a : b) = 1;
> > > }
> > 
> > This is a gcc extension. You can look in the info pages to see what gcc has
> > as extensions, or you can use the -ansi flag on gcc to get it to issue
> > warnings about its own extensions.
